WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:06.729
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this is going
to be my Doctor Who Finale Review and a breakdown

00:00:06.729 --> 00:00:10.769
of the Christmas Special Trailer.

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:16.000
A bunch of you have already asked me on twitter
about some of the big moments imply about

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.880
next year and series 9 so I’ll try to address
all those.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.819
Real Quick reminder, the weekly giveaway regenerates
right now. All you have to do to enter is

00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:29.130
be a subscriber and leave a comment on the
video. Feel free to leave 10 comments. There

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:29.769
was enough happening to make everyone go crazy.

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:33.250
Careful for spoilers if you’re not caught
up. But Starting with Top 10 moments.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:39.630
Number 10 - Doctor Clara Rule Number 1

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:46.630
Lots of Doctor Clara Lying, it explained the
“Clara never existed” line. And yes that

00:00:54.750 --> 00:01:01.750
was the 
Danny Cyberman in the special office box.
Number 9 - Cybermen Everywhere and No One

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:09.990
Cares

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:16.829
This was a continuation of the final moment
from last week and the children in the forest

00:01:16.829 --> 00:01:23.829
in episode 10 being completely unimpressed
with scary things.

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:26.560
Number 8 - UNIT Is Back

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:33.560
So many things, Osgood with the Bowtie, Kate
Stewart with the Mondas 

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:48.119
Cyberman Head.

00:01:57.459 --> 00:02:00.549
Number 7 - Cybermen Weather Forecast

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:05.109
When Missy explained they were pollenating,
the cyber conversion process goes like this.

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:09.399
Cyberman explodes in the air spreading a giant
cloud of nanites, nanites bond with water

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:16.020
molecules in the air, rain down and start
cyber converting organic matter. Namely the

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:16.710
dead.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:23.710
Which is why it jumped to Chaplet Funeral
Home, I believe this was a reference to Dodo

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:27.470
Chaplet. Who was a companion towards the end
of the first Doctor’s run.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:31.860
The critical step is Missy downloading all
the stored minds from the data cloud into

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.360
the cyber converted bodies.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.230
If she didn’t do that, it would be a bunch
of lifeless cybermen. Which she was controlling

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:36.460
with the wrist bracelet.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.040
Number 6 - Doctor President of Earth

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.400
I feel like they crammed more references to
classic who in this scene than almost anywhere

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.870
else. There’s the Brigadier Painting, the
fact that the Fourth Doctor was President

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:50.290
of The Time Lords for a brief period, I think
that was also during the middle of a Master

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:50.710
arc.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:55.620
I heard a Thunderbirds shout out. And the
setup for the Doctor never saluting the Brigadier,

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.340
which they did pay off at the end.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.680
Number 5 - Missy Teases Gallifrey

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:07.460
As we all expected, Gallifrey was mentioned.
Missy’s explanation leaves a lot to be desired.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:11.090
The way it’s written leaves a lot of room
for interpretation. She kind of waves her

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.640
hand at the mechanics.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:18.140
But here’s what I gathered. The Doctor saved
Gallifrey during the 50th. So all of the events

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:22.440
of End of Time were nullified. Everyone, including
Rassilon were incorporated into this new Capaldi

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.820
Even though it seemed like the coordinates
were bogus, Gallifrey is still in the pocket

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.170
universe. Along with Rassilon and everyone
else that didn’t die during the time war

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.040
before the events of the 50th.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.150
As for the explanation of her escape. Here
are two possibilities.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:32.770
We know she has a TARDIS, which I think is
the red phone booth. She could have found

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.860
a way to pilot it out of the pocket universe
that the other timelords haven’t discovered

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.930
yet. She could just be more clever.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.910
Or she could be this person here, climbing
out of the painting during the 50th. It looks

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.090
like a Woman’s hand grabbing the frame from
the inside of the painting.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.020
Those are just two theories about how she
escaped, so if you have a different one just

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:47.700
write it in the comment.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.560
I think she regenerated after the end of time,
sometime during the 50th while that was all

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:48.670
going down.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:52.020
Number 4 - Missy Destroys Everyone on the
Plane and Leaves the Doctor Mid-Air

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:59.020
I love that she was waiting for him to go
splat and regenerate. Even though there was

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.860
a whole Matrix vibe coming off last week and
that was a classic who story involving the

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:10.380
stealing of regenerations. I felt like they
way Moffat wrote Missy, she didn’t seem

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.270
like she cared about regenerations.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:18.069
A lot of you hypothesized in the comments
that Missy is somewhere around her fourth

00:04:18.069 --> 00:04:20.209
regeneration and Capaldi is the beginning
of a new cycle too. So neither of them are

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:22.650
super worried about dying.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.720
Although the whole Doctor mid-air TARDIS entry
Squee thing was funny.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.389
Totally not surprised they had Missy vaporize
SEB. Even though the Squee was a little too

00:04:29.389 --> 00:04:31.660
much, I laughed.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:38.660
I’m really bummed that Osgood is dead. And
even though they saved Kate I think Osgood

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:46.350
is gone. They just wanted to not bring the
character back so they killed her off.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:53.350
Really nice that Missy called her pretty and
tried to boost her self esteem before doing

00:04:55.220 --> 00:05:01.460
the deed.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.000
Number 3 - Danny Pink Cyberman Feels

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.270
Appropriately Horrific reveal when he pulled
the facemask off. I feel like we knew it was

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:11.350
going to be him from the minute we saw the
crumpled up paper earlier in the episode.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.130
But still stung a bit when we saw his face.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:15.520
It reminded me of the Dalek Oswin reveal at
the end of Asylum, where we see the human

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:16.900
face inside the Dalek.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:22.550
I still feel like that moment is a level of
scary that series 8 never quite matched. Dalek

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:26.310
Oswin way more frightening to watch than Cyberman
Danny Pink.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:30.350
Totally not surprised that he had a level
of control over the other Cybermen, even though

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:36.200
the Doctor could have probably done the same
thing himself with the control bracelet.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:40.960
Couple of other Graveyard favorites including
the gravestones of Amy, Rory and Victorian

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:41.850
Clara.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:46.060
There had been a rumor of an Amy Rory Cyberman
scene, and I’m actually kind of glad it

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:49.750
wasn’t in there. I feel like it would have
been too much with them already doing the

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.590
Brigadier Cyberman moment.

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:54.380
Number 2 - The Master Explains Everything

00:05:54.380 --> 00:06:01.240
I just want my friend back, best reason to
destroy the human race ever.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:06.560
Michelle Gomez did an amazing job of being
sympathetic, I really felt like her version

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:13.560
of The Master desperately wanted her best
friend back but because of the sound of drums,

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:18.340
she’d been twisted to the point of insanity.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:22.490
She didn’t even care what the Council of
Time Lords would do to her when they got back

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:25.960
to gallifrey. That’s how bad she wanted
the Doctor back.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:31.199
Michelle Gomez wins this episode, always.
I really do think she’s amazing. I can’t

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:35.389
wait to see how Moffat explains her surviving,
the next time she shows up.

00:06:35.389 --> 00:06:40.010
And yes, I definitely think she’ll be back
at some point. Maybe not the Christmas Special

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.320
and but hopefully at some point during Series
9.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:46.389
I feel like she’ll continue to be tied to
the Gallifrey Plot regardless of whatever

00:06:46.389 --> 00:06:47.770
her next big scheme is.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:50.790
As for the actual coordinates she gave the
Doctor. I think Moffat will explain that in

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:54.160
Series 9. It seemed like she was lying. The
Doctor smashed the console because he was

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:54.300
pissed.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:58.990
It’s possible that Missy just omitted some
critical piece of information or The Doctor

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:01.970
was being a pudding brain and misinterpreted
what she was saying.

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:06.860
And my Number 1 WTF Moment - Clara is Leaving
and The Christmas Special Teaser

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:11.930
Starting with Clara, I understand the Danny
Pink end credits scene, I understand why they

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:16.210
wrote it that way. Giving his character a
sad but hopeful ending.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:19.680
I think the reason they left Clara alive but
kept Danny Pink dead was to not do the exact

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:22.540
same thing they did with Amy and Rory. They
wanted a simliar sad ending but didn’t want

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.220
to completely recycle Amy’s ending by having
Clara jump into the void.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:27.760
And they had to lay the groundwork for a new
companion coming on. Which could totally happen

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:32.280
during the christmas special or in the first
episode of series 9.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.820
They made the queen joke about a female doctor,
totally think that will happen during our

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:36.880
lifetimes, just not in the next regeneration.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:40.240
Let me know though, what was your favorite
moment and do you think we’ll see the next

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:41.320
companion during the christmas special?

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.570
I fully expect Capaldi to stay on until Moffat
Leaves. Which could be as early as Series

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:49.520
10. It’s possible Moffat will leave after
series 9. It’s too soon for him to go now

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.870
because they probably started writing scripts
for it.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:54.900
Series 9 will probably premiere around the
same time next year, which means they’d

00:07:54.900 --> 00:08:00.080
have to start filming early next year and
in order to do that, they’d have to have

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.830
finished scripts ready to go by the end of
this year.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.320
Moffat is a busy man, they’re also shooting
the Sherlock 2015 christmas special in January.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:11.660
So after they finish shooting that I think
they’ll start shooting series 9.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:16.729
Now to address the Christmas Special Footage.
Yes that was Nick Frost as Santa Claus at

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:16.960
the end.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:21.639
In the teaser image they released of him,
he’s wearing a futuristic looking uniform,

00:08:21.639 --> 00:08:26.290
so either he’s a humanoid alien playing
Santa or he’s going to be someone from earth’s

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.050
future playing Santa.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:32.479
Christmas Episodes deal with Christmas as
an event, so I think that explains the santa

00:08:32.479 --> 00:08:35.479
suit. But I’ve seen a lot of you theorize
that the episode is going to present santa

00:08:35.479 --> 00:08:40.969
claus as a real person. Like he exists, it’s
not just a character people dress up as.

00:08:40.969 --> 00:08:44.680
The location will be a research station at
the north pole. When the Doctor said that

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:49.820
I thought of Ice Station Zebra, the Cold War
Movie from the 60s. The creature looks like

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.760
it could be an Ice Warrior without it’s
armor.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:56.500
Sometimes they spoil those things in the trailers.
They’ll probably release more clips and

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.980
images in the next couple of weeks.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:03.490
We’ve only got about 7 weeks, so just expect
new things from the BBC at least once a week.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:09.399
So just to rank the finale against the other
recent finales I’ll give it a B plus. And

00:09:09.399 --> 00:09:12.820
when I’m comparing it to other finales I’m
just trying to judge it based on Eccleston,

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.390
Tennant and Smith’s first finale.

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:19.510
Peter Capaldi has only had one season so it’s
kind of unfair to judge this finale against

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:25.080
Matt Smith’s or tennant’s third seasons.
The more time you get to spend with each doctor,

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:29.800
the more precious they become, the more rewarding
finales become.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:36.800
So let’s just stick to each doctor’s first
finale. I still think Eccleston’s is the

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:45.020
best, then The Series 5 Finale, Then the series
2 finale. Death in Heaven didn’t quite nail

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:53.260
the dismount but I love it for bringing back
The Master in a really interesting way.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:10:00.000
I just feel like it had to much extra baggage
to deal with. You have a brand new doctor,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:07.000
another doctor’s companion leaving and a
gender swapped fan favorite character being

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:12.310
introduced. All in a season when almost every
major plot point was leaked.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:16.410
In all fairness, Matt Smith originally had
intended to stay on for Series 8 but then

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:20.630
changed his mind early last year causing the
BBC to scramble to find a new Doctor. That

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:25.700
created the unusual situation where you have
a brand new companion coming and going in

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:26.440
the span of two seasons.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:28.350
I feel like the transition completely overshadowed
our ability to connect with Clara as a companion.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:34.140
I think it was a lot easier to bond with Amy
Pond because she was introduced at the same

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:37.100
time as Matt Smith was, they even brought
her back for his regeneration scene. Arguably

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.740
the current companion should be the only companion
on screen when a doctor regenerates.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:46.500
Just a little messy there, but all in all
I am very excited for the Christmas Special

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:49.000
and what Series 9 has in store.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.399
I will do a separate series 9 predictions
video, so be sure to subscribe to get that.

00:10:53.399 --> 00:10:57.980
My Q&amp;A for the finale will post tomorrow.
So please ask all your Missy, Gallifrey, Christmas

00:10:57.980 --> 00:10:58.870
Special questions.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:04.060
Right now click here to get that and click
here for my Episode 11 video.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.890
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and I’ll see you guys tonight!

